LOGBOOK.md-1804-- DECISION: the two quarantine-ENOSPC recoveries have a different SHAPE and the tests now say so at the case. A candidate that was never a valid object cannot install on retry, so its recovery is that it is preserved as evidence exactly as it would have been without the fault. A corrupt existing object is deliberately left at the digest path, so its recovery is what the NEXT run does with it still there.
