LOGBOOK.md-1813-- FINDING: `PutBlob` folded the staged-LENGTH comparison into the same condition as the two source-IDENTITY comparisons: `info.Size() < 0 || uint64(info.Size()) != actualSize || actualSize != expectedSize || actualDigest != expected`. The identity terms compare what the source produced against what the caller declared, which is the SPEC.md Section 3.2 quarantine trigger. The length term compares what the copy ACCEPTED against what the filesystem KEPT, which proves nothing about the source bytes at all. This is the exact write-side mirror of the read-side defect recorded at 2030 today, in the same function, and it survived that fix.
LOGBOOK.md-1814-- FINDING: on a delayed-allocation filesystem (ext4, XFS, APFS) ENOSPC surfaces at writeback, not at the accepting write. So the disagreement is reachable with NO error raised on either side: `io.Copy` reports the full length, the hasher agrees with the declared digest, and only `fstat` disagrees.
