LOGBOOK.md-1812-
LOGBOOK.md-1813-- FINDING: `PutBlob` folded the staged-LENGTH comparison into the same condition as the two source-IDENTITY comparisons: `info.Size() < 0 || uint64(info.Size()) != actualSize || actualSize != expectedSize || actualDigest != expected`. The identity terms compare what the source produced against what the caller declared, which is the SPEC.md Section 3.2 quarantine trigger. The length term compares what the copy ACCEPTED against what the filesystem KEPT, which proves nothing about the source bytes at all. This is the exact write-side mirror of the read-side defect recorded at 2030 today, in the same function, and it survived that fix.
LOGBOOK.md-1814-- FINDING: on a delayed-allocation filesystem (ext4, XFS, APFS) ENOSPC surfaces at writeback, not at the accepting write. So the disagreement is reachable with NO error raised on either side: `io.Copy` reports the full length, the hasher agrees with the declared digest, and only `fstat` disagrees.
LOGBOOK.md-1815-- ROOT CAUSE of the consequence: a fragment was installed into quarantine and reported with `PutResult.Digest`/`Size` describing bytes no artifact on disk held — the digest of the full source attached to a truncated file. An incident record built from that result would name a digest that does not match the quarantined bytes. Second consequence: a full volume made the store write MORE data, into quarantine, on the volume whose exhaustion caused the fault.
LOGBOOK.md-1816-- FIX: `internal/localstore/object_store.go:219` — the condition is split. A staged-length disagreement returns `ErrDurability` with no quarantine path and a zero `PutResult`; the fragment is discarded by the existing deferred cleanup. `README.md` now says "size or digest mismatches OF THE SOURCE BYTES" are quarantined.
LOGBOOK.md-1817-- DECISION: write-side faults are driven through the PRE-EXISTING `storeOperations.syncFile` seam, not a new one. fsync is where a real ENOSPC is discovered, so a failure raised there and a length that changed by stat time are the two shapes the condition actually takes. No new production seam was added to the object store.
