LOGBOOK.md-1829-- ROOT CAUSE: `validateSessionLaunchPlan` and `internal/config`'s `validateExtensions` both measured a declared 65,536-byte bound with `len(json.Marshal(value))`. `encoding/json` rewrites each of the single bytes `<`, `>` and `&` into a six-character escape, and U+2028/U+2029 from three canonical bytes into six, so the bound in force was up to 6x tighter than the pinned one and was a property of `encoding/json` rather than of the specification. It failed closed — nothing oversized was admitted — but a CONFORMING document was refused, and the third site, `validateExtensionsObject`, already measured canonical bytes. One repository carried both the defect and its fix.
LOGBOOK.md-1830-- FINDING: `SetEscapeHTML(false)` alone does NOT fix it. `encoding/json` escapes U+2028 and U+2029 regardless of that setting, so only the RFC 8785 transform makes the measurement independent of the encoder. Probed directly: `["<"]` is 5 canonical bytes and 10 marshalled; `[U+2028]` is 7 canonical and 10 marshalled.
LOGBOOK.md-1831-- FIX: `internal/canonicaljson/declared_byte_bounds.go` — `CanonicalByteLength` (encode with `SetEscapeHTML(false)`, then `Canonicalize`) is the one measurement, and `canonicalByteBound(name, value, maximum)` is the one refusal gate. `closed_shapes.go:284` and `closed_shapes.go:1794` call the gate; `internal/config/validation.go:763` calls the measurement. `internal/config` now imports `internal/canonicaljson`; no cycle, canonicaljson imports only `catalog` and `scalar`.
