LOGBOOK.md-1884-### 2240 — A pinned vocabulary set does not pin the JSON path that reaches it
LOGBOOK.md-1885-
LOGBOOK.md-1886-- FINDING: `testdata/closed-vocabularies.md` pins the admitted set of all 47 production vocabulary call sites and kills any widening mutant at the source. It says nothing about WHICH member each gate is reached from. A validator that read a Lease Record `reason` through the `session.quiescing` reason gate would leave every pinned row byte-identical while admitting `stop` on a lease. The pin is over the source, the defect is over the wiring.
LOGBOOK.md-1887-- FIX: `internal/canonicaljson/record_conformance_test.go` walks every closed-vocabulary position of every identity fixture — 149 positions — and feeds each the union of every OTHER pinned vocabulary, 14,639 substitutions, requiring refusal outside that position's own declared set. Positions are found by VALUE, not by a member-name list, so a new enum in a new record is swept without being registered anywhere.
LOGBOOK.md-1888-- ANOMALY, and the reason the first version of this sweep was worthless: keying the declared set by member NAME let the widening mutant through. `reason` is declared twice — Lease Record `{create, graceful_takeover, force_takeover, recovery}` and `session.quiescing` `{graceful_takeover, stop, checkpoint}` — so the member-name union already contained `stop` and the sweep never substituted it. Mutant M3 SURVIVED the first run. Same shape for `kind` (session vs Transfer Manifest) and `materialization_policy` (git vs managed_tree member).
LOGBOOK.md-1889-- FIX: the declared set is now the single pinned row whose member AND admitted values contain the fixture's own value, with candidates deduplicated by admitted set so six identical `execution_profile` rows count as one vocabulary. The four genuinely ambiguous positions carry a reviewed resolution that must remain one of the candidate rows, so a widened production vocabulary invalidates the resolution instead of being absorbed by it, and a stale resolution naming no position is reported.
LOGBOOK.md-1890-- NOTE: a position whose value matches NO row for its member is an exact-literal site, not a vocabulary — `clone.failed` pins `phase=checkpoint` while `clone.target_validation_failed` carries a six-member `phase` enum. It is swept as a single-value set, which is the stronger bound, rather than skipped. Free strings that coincidentally hold a pinned value (a manifest entry whose `path` is literally `file`) fall out because no pinned row declares their member.
