LOGBOOK.md-1934-- ROOT CAUSE: `validateMesh` (`internal/config/validation.go:449`) bounded `mesh.peers[].endpoint` only with `validatePrintableCharacters(…, 1, 1024)`. The Section 6.3 bypass gate reads `ssh_args` and nothing else, and SPEC.md:2494 hands `ssh(1)` the endpoint as an atomic argv value — but an atomic argv value is not a destination, because `ssh(1)` reads its destination positionally through getopt.
LOGBOOK.md-1935-- FINDING: reproduced at the production `loadConfigDocument` entry with a 34-shape hostile-endpoint probe. Against the pre-fix base (an archive of checkpoint `10aaa16`) 32 of 34 loaded with `err=nil`, including `endpoint = "-oStrictHostKeyChecking=no"`, `"-oUserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null"`, `"-F/attacker/config"`, `"-J jump.example"`, `"--"`, and `"peer.example -oStrictHostKeyChecking=no"`. The first two are exactly the bypass Section 6.3 requires refusing, reached through a field the ssh_args gate never inspects. Only the tab and newline shapes were already refused, one clause earlier by the printable-character bound. After the fix all 34 are refused and every option-shaped one names the `option-like value` clause. Probe logs: `.temp/BUG-260902-4ajzyz/audit-probe-before-01.log` and `-after-01.log`.
LOGBOOK.md-1936-- FIX: `internal/config/endpoint.go` admits the field against a closed `[user@]host[:port]` grammar — leading `-` and any whitespace refused first by name, then a 1-64 character login name, LDH DNS labels or a bracketed IPv6 literal, and a decimal port in 1-65535. Wired as one new refusal site at `validation.go:453`, clause `mesh.peers[N].endpoint <reason>`.
LOGBOOK.md-1937-- DECISION: the grammar is deliberately narrower than every destination `ssh(1)` accepts (no bare IPv6, no trailing dot, no `%zone`, LDH labels only). Fail-closed is the point: widening it is a reviewed change, not an accident. A bare IPv6 literal is refused specifically because its colons are indistinguishable from the port separator.
LOGBOOK.md-1938-- FINDING: the dangling `-o` the audit reported as admitted was already closed by BUG-260902-beqfwr — `admitSSHArguments` returns `sshRefusalMissingFlagValue` for it today. Verified by probe, then pinned per declared value-taking letter (`-i -l -p -o`, alone, grouped as `-q<letter>`, and as a trailing argument) rather than left as the two incidental cases it had.
LOGBOOK.md-1939-- FINDING: the disclosed short-flag asymmetry is real and is what let `-A`, `-E` and `-L` mutants pass green: `TestLoadRefusesEverySSHShortOptionOutsideThePermittedTables` skips whatever production permits, so a mutant that permits a letter deletes its own subtest. Closed with the both-directions key-set pin `permittedSSHOptionSamples` already gave the `-o` registry, plus named assertions for the capability-widening letters `-A -E -L -R -D -W -w -S -O`.
LOGBOOK.md-1940-- REGRESSION: `schema_test.go`'s endpoint bound used `strings.Repeat("界", 1024)`, which the grammar refuses; rewritten as `strings.Repeat("a.", 511) + "ab"` so the 1024-character bound stays reachable through the grammar and is still proved at 1024 accepted / 1025 refused.
