LOGBOOK.md-2098-- ROOT CAUSE: `ProjectionMetadata.SourceFingerprint` was asserted only against itself across three opens of the same source. A constant is maximally self-consistent, so replacing `projectionSourceFingerprint` with `"sha256:" + hex(make([]byte, 32))` satisfied every existing assertion. The whole fingerprint chain — and the scan ordering feeding it — was reachable, exercised, and unfalsifiable.
LOGBOOK.md-2099-- FINDING: The determinism test read digest order back through `Objects()`, which carries its own `ORDER BY storage_class, representation, digest`. The loop that looked like it pinned the production `sort.Slice` was decided by the read query in a different function. This is the round-6/7 sibling-decider shape again, one step further out: the decider is not a preceding line or a sibling term but a re-sort on the read path.
LOGBOOK.md-2100-- DECISION: Derive the expected fingerprint *outside the module*. `.temp/TASK-260830-3amrl9/fingerprint-derivation.py` re-implements it in Python and executes no Go production code, so the golden cannot be a copy of what the implementation emits today. It independently reproduced the reviewer's probe value exactly.
