# BUG-260917-2fwf8e results

## Scope and identity

- Task: `BUG-260917-2fwf8e`, developer handoff from Story worktree.
- Base checkpoint: `799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2`.
- Candidate: current managed Story worktree, intentionally UNCOMMITTED.
- Scope: `internal/fencing.Authorize` arm ordering and its
  `terminstance.ObserveFencing` composition. No lease-chain implementation
  or Section 5.2 park vocabulary was changed.

## Acceptance coverage

3 of 3 task Acceptance Criteria rows are driven through named production
entries:

1. `fencing.Authorize` now resolves ownership direction before consuming a
   lapsed-grant result. A remote interactive owner returns the existing
   `remote_owner` park with `not_owner`; `axpane.Decide` reaches
   `attach_remote` or `takeover_offer`, never `lease_conflict`.
2. The committed `N-arm-order-expiry-before-direction` mutant swaps the two
   arms while preserving both gates and kills both
   `TestAuthorizeRemoteInteractiveOwnerLapsedGrantUsesRemoteOfferArm` and
   `TestAuthorizeLapsedRemoteOwnerUsesDirectionForEveryEntry`.
3. The exact report-only reviewer probe body was run on the base and
   candidate, with before/after logs and neighbouring vectors attached.

Production-entry coverage is 5 of 5 `Authorize` operation entries in the
lapsed-remote census (activation, restore, input, mutation, checkpoint), plus
the composed `axpane.Decide` `ModeLaunch`/`AuthorizeActivation` row. The local
lapsed stale-token negative also drives all 5 entries. Wrapper coverage is 3
of 3 required outcomes: interactive attach, interactive takeover, and
non-interactive park.

## Before/after probe evidence

The probe sources are under `probes/`; the corresponding logs are under
`logs/` in the attached evidence archive.

| Input | Base checkpoint | Candidate | Interpretation |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Probe 10: remote interactive owner + lapsed local grant | `refused/lease_conflict` | `attach_remote`, `remote_owner`, `not_owner` | §4.2 step-4 offer path is reachable. |
| V01: remote winner + lapsed grant | all five `REFUSE(lease_conflict)` | activation/restore `PARK(remote_owner,not_owner)`; input/mutation/checkpoint `REFUSE(not_owner)` | Ownership direction is now consulted before expiry. |
| V07: remote winner + lapsed grant + stale epoch | all five `REFUSE(lease_conflict)` | same split as V01 | Stale token remains a refusal/park at the direct gate; composition fences it. |
| V08: remote winner + lapsed grant + same-epoch loser | all five `REFUSE(lease_conflict)` | same split as V01 | Losing lease is not hidden by expiry. |
| V09: remote winner + lapsed grant + future epoch | all five `REFUSE(lease_conflict)` | same split as V01 | Future token remains non-authorizing. |
| V14: remote winner + lapsed grant + empty `LocalHostID` | all five `REFUSE(lease_conflict)` | same split as V01 | Remote direction is explicit, not inferred from a local-host default. |

Neighbour vectors are driven and recorded:

- Live local grant: direct `Authorize` mints the exact winning token.
- Remote non-interactive owner: `axpane.Decide` returns `parked(remote_owner)`
  without an offer/runtime.
- Local owner with a lapsed grant: direct `Authorize` remains literal
  `lease_conflict` on all five entries.
- Remote unusable policy remains `invalid_arguments`; policy validity was not
  weakened by the ordering fix.

The stale-composition repair is separately pinned by
`TestObserveFencingRemoteWinnerLapsedGrantFencesStaleIncarnation`: stale
epoch and same-epoch losing tokens from active, parked, and quiescing states
transition to literal `stale_fenced`. Winning and future tokens remain the
existing remote park with no transition. The old property probe is also green
on the base because the old outer fallback still caught the refusal; the new
committed test is the important post-fix case where the direct question now
returns `remote_owner` before the relative question defers expiry.

## Full importer-set outcome diff

Per-test JSON output was normalized to TSV for the full importer set
`internal/fencing/...`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/axpane`, and
`internal/termbind`:

| Package | Base rows | Candidate rows | New rows | Existing status changes |
