| `internal/fencing` | 310 | 328 | 18 | 0 |
| `internal/terminstance` | 303 | 310 | 7 | 0 |
| `internal/axpane` | 195 | 200 | 5 | 0 |
| `internal/termbind` | 265 | 265 | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **1,073** | **1,103** | **30** | **0** |

The 30-row addition is the committed direct, entry-census, wrapper, local
boundary, and composition coverage. The semantic movements of V01/V07/V08/
V09/V14 are named above and in `outcomes/per-test-diff.tsv`; they are not
hidden by the unchanged pass total. Running the base tests against candidate
production intentionally fails in the old `fencing_grantless_test.go` rows
that asserted expiry-first direct behavior, which confirms the moved contract;
the candidate test suite is green after those assertions were split into the
direct offer and composed stale-fence expectations.

## Negative and mutation evidence

- Fencing battery: `mutants-fencing-full-v3` returned rc 0; 31 narrowing
  `N-` rows and the token-preserving `T-census-alias` were KILLED. The
  harmless control SURVIVED; NOT_APPLIED and compile-failure controls remain
