 - EVIDENCE: `TestAuthorizeRemoteInteractiveOwnerLapsedGrantUsesRemoteOfferArm` drives `Authorize`; `TestAuthorizeLapsedRemoteOwnerUsesDirectionForEveryEntry` drives all five entries; `TestAuthorizeLapsedLocalOwnerStaleTokenRemainsLeaseConflict` attacks the local-lapsed boundary; `TestDecideLapsedRemoteOwnerOffersOrParksByInteractiveContext` drives `axpane.Decide` in restore and launch modes. Neighbours are live local grant → authorized, remote non-interactive owner → parked `remote_owner`, and local lapsed grant → `lease_conflict`; invalid policy remains `invalid_arguments`.
 - SUITE DIFF: the four importer packages were compared per test: baseline 1,073 PASS rows (`fencing` 310, `terminstance` 303, `axpane` 195, `termbind` 265) versus candidate 1,103 PASS rows (`328`, `310`, `200`, `265`). The normalized diff is 30 new named rows and zero existing status changes; the moved V01/V07/V08/V09/V14 inputs are recorded separately because their semantic output changed without a test failure.
-- MUTATION: fencing `mutants-full-v3` killed all 31 narrowing rows plus the token-preserving `T-census-alias`; `N-arm-order-expiry-before-direction` fails both the direct and all-entry regressions. Terminstance `mutants-terminstance-full-v4` killed 120 narrowing rows plus the one labelled tightening row; the lapsed fallback narrowing and the winning/future no-transition narrowing both fail, with the harmless control surviving. The old equivalent `N-fencing-operation-remote` row was retired and re-anchored composition is now named `N-fencing-remote-lapsed-not-stale`. No `__pycache__`/`.pyc` artifacts.
-- VALIDATION: targeted importer tests, both mutation batteries, the configured 30-command suite, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, and the race/coverage lanes all exited 0. `cataloggen -check` printed 180 `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics but exited 0; the raw output is retained rather than hidden.
