LOGBOOK.md:10:- SCOPE: `internal/fencing.Authorize` arm precedence plus the required `terminstance.ObserveFencing` composition repair. `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` remains the expiry owner; no lease-chain code or Section 5.2 park vocabulary changed. The direct question exposes the existing `remote_owner` park, while the composed relative question still fences stale incarnations through `StaleRelativeToWinner` when deferred expiry would otherwise hide the tuple verdict.
LOGBOOK.md-11-- REPRO: the exact report-only probe bodies from `TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz` were replayed against checkpoint `799c338e` and the candidate. Before: probe 10 returned `refused/lease_conflict`; after: `attach_remote`, `remote_owner`, `not_owner`. Direct V01 was `REFUSE(lease_conflict)` on all five entries before and `PARK(remote_owner,not_owner)` on activation/restore plus `REFUSE(not_owner)` on input/mutation/checkpoint after. V07/V08/V09/V14 moved identically and are named in the results.
LOGBOOK.md:12:- FIX: policy validity is still refused as `invalid_arguments` before direction; only `fencing_grant_expired` is deferred. A remote winner therefore returns the existing `remote_owner` park, making v0.7.0 §4.2 step-4 attach/takeover reachable. `observeRemoteWinner` now adds a grant-independent `StaleRelativeToWinner` fallback for the relative lapsed-grant question: stale epoch/losing lease fences to literal `stale_fenced`, while winning/future tokens remain parked. A local lapsed grant remains `lease_conflict`.
