/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-92-## Story Detailing (MANDATORY before phase planning)
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-93-
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-94-- **The Orchestrator details settled scope inline:** read each Story, create its atomic Tasks/Bugs, write complete descriptions and acceptance criteria, and link dependencies directly through `task-board`. Do not create a decomposition meta-task or spawn `solution-architect` merely to copy settled requirements into the board.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md:95:- Set the Story to `analysis` while its board shape is being refined: `task-board m 'set_status(STORY-260218-abc, status=analysis)'`.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-96-- Read and refine it until the description, scope, AC, leaves, and dependency edges are unambiguous:
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-97-  - `task-board q --format compact 'get(STORY-260218-abc) { id name status description scope ac children blockedBy derivedBlockedBy }'`
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-98-  - `task-board m 'create(type=task, parent=STORY-260218-abc, name=..., description="...")'`
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-99-  - `task-board m 'set_details(TASK-260218-def, scope="...", ac="...")'`
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-100-  - `task-board m 'link(TASK-260218-def, blocked_by=TASK-260218-abc)'`
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md:101:- Each Task/Bug should be atomic: one clear specialist deliverable with verifiable AC and task-specific checklist items.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-102-- Do not create a single-task Story or a single-Story Epic: its only child's `done` cascade-promotes an otherwise-unfinished parent straight into the commit-confirmation gate (see [statuses](statuses.md#commit-confirmation-for-accepted-work)). Put research/analysis work as a Task among sibling Tasks in a Story instead, so a container's aggregate status reflects real sibling progress rather than one child accidentally carrying it.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-103-- **Implementation-first vertical slices are the default.** Detail a Story so that its first leaf drives real behaviour end to end — parser plus evaluator plus one real adapter, owner registration plus store plus isolation — and later leaves widen it. Do not detail a framework, a general harness, or a full operation table first: a 72-operation framework leaf is not a slice, and "actual behaviour" means a production entry point exercised, not a touched file or a mock.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-104-- **Research leaves are bounded and serial depth is one.** A research Task exists only for a decision the spec leaves open (`solution-architect` rule 4) and carries the plan contract in [research workflow](research-workflow.md#research-plan-contract-bounded-by-default): the decision, the smallest frozen grammar/vector precondition for the NEXT runtime slice where applicable, worker-time and artifact budgets, exit criteria, and the first production slice that consumes it. A second serial research prerequisite is an escalation trigger: re-scope toward implementation or record a justified budget extension with the named unresolved decision. A prerequisite justified by consistency alone is refused (row R1 of [negative evidence](negative-evidence.md#refusal-rows-research-and-validation-budgets)).
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-105-- **Freeze only what the next slice consumes.** `solution-architect` rule 7 freezes the grammar revision the next runtime slice implements, not the whole system, and does not add a generic conformance harness as a prerequisite by default. Distinguish prototype work, where the grammar may still move behind a stated bound, from compatibility work, where an external consumer fixes it. A security or interoperability requirement may widen the freeze, with the concrete reason written in the leaf.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-106-- Spawn `solution-architect` only when detailing is blocked on a genuine architecture decision, such as a cross-module contract or system-design tradeoff. The Orchestrator routes decomposition quality checks through that tracked decision task, for example `task-board spawn STORY-260218-abc --role solution-architect --background`; the child produces the decision, and the Orchestrator still applies it to the board inline. Settled-scope decomposition itself remains inline Orchestrator work.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md:107:- After detailing, set the Story to `to-dev`, not `done`: `task-board m 'set_status(STORY-260218-abc, status=to-dev)'`. `done` means accepted implementation, not completed decomposition.
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-108-- **Do NOT proceed to Phase Planning until all stories have tasks**
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-109-- This ensures the plan shows the real scope of work
/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/references/planning-workflow.md-110-
